      "seed": 766472713,
      "version": 390,
      "versionNonce": 183849319,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782094634489,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In programming Array is a collection of multiple values.\n\nfeatures of Array\n=================\n\n1.Array is a collection of similar type.\n\n2. Array is an object in java .\n\n3.Array is created in runtime.\n\n4.it lives in heap area.\n\n5.We need a reference to access an array.\n\n6.Array is created using \"new\" keword.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In programming Array is a collection of multiple values.\n\nfeatures of Array\n=================\n\n1.Array is a collection of similar type.\n\n2. Array is an object in java .\n\n3.Array is created in runtime.\n\n4.it lives in heap area.\n\n5.We need a reference to access an array.\n\n6.Array is created using \"new\" keword.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Dy62gsK7O8WuDjBGSMslB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 298,
      "y": 669.8333325386047,
      "width": 363,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
